```javascript
function unique(items) {
  const seen = new Set();
  const out = [];
  for (const item of items) {
    if (!seen.has(item)) {
      seen.add(item);
      out.push(item);
    }
  }
  return out;
}
```
A set records what has already been seen, so each value is kept the first time it appears and skipped afterwards. Insertion order is preserved and the whole pass is O(n).

```javascript
function sum(numbers) {
  return numbers.reduce((total, n) => total + n, 0);
}
```
reduce folds the array into a single value, starting from 0 so an empty array returns 0 rather than undefined.
